=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/DiskForecast (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/DiskForecast   kind=page   web route=/admin/disk-forecast
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/DiskForecastPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  SchemaDriftPage / VehicleCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "DiskForecastPage.xaml +
  DiskForecastPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("DiskForecast", already in RouteTable.cs →
  /admin/disk-forecast, group AdminDevTools). DiskForecastPage shares the FeatureViews.Admin namespace with the
  sibling pages and reuses their internal JsonReadHelpers (no duplicate type).
- W1 predecessor (ADR-004): the generated C# OpenAPI client (apps/windows/Generated/, namespace
  TeslaSync.Windows.Generated.Api) is gitignored ("regenerated, not committed"). It was materialized locally via the
  documented codegen — npx tsx@4.22.4 apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts (10 C# files) — plus the thin
  Generated/Generated.csproj wrapper the App.Core/App.Tests project references resolve. This is a local build
  prerequisite only; it is NOT part of the commit (the directory stays gitignored).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useDiskForecast (GET /admin/observability/disk-forecast). The
  view-model reads through an injected IDiskForecastFeed; the default EmptyDiskForecastFeed resolves the empty state
  (matching the sibling host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed DiskForecastClientFeed
  (DiskForecastPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract client operation
  get_api_v1_admin_observability_disk_forecast (no params), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches
  the view. A non-success response surfaces as ApiException; the view-model maps StatusCode==503 to the distinct
  subsystem-unavailable banner (web `subsystemMissing`) and every other failure to the generic InfoBar+Retry.
- The web page renders all regions INSIDE the PageContainer body (PageContainer is passed only `query=` for the
  freshness chip, not loading/error/empty), so the native port reproduces the four data states as visible Fluent
  regions per ADR-006: loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(4) shimmer; error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry;
  503 subsystem-missing -> TsAlertBanner(Warning) notConfigured; empty -> TsGlassPanel + TsEmptyState; success ->
  the four fleet-totals StatCards + the hypertables table. Never a blank region.
- SI / display boundary (P1/S5): the on-wire fields are SI byte counts (int64 total/uncompressed/compressed,
  float64 growth_bytes_per_day), an int chunk_count and a nullable int est_days_to_quota. Bytes format through
  FormatBytes (the web formatBytes: B verbatim < 1 KiB, then KB/MB/GB at one fixed decimal); the days estimate
  through NumberFormatting (web fmtNumber at getGlobalPrecision()==2); percentages via toFixed(1). The severity
  badge maps the wire tier through StatusKind (ok→Success, warn→Warning, critical→Danger, unknown→Neutral) with the
  web SEVERITY_LABEL text (OK/Warn/Critical/—) — the web's own non-i18n constants, kept verbatim.
- All 23 i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names: 22 new
  translation.admin.diskForecast.* added to Strings/en/Resources.resw (alphabetically placed before the dlq block) +
  the pre-existing translation.admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle (shared with SchemaDrift, not duplicated). The
  ar/he catalogs lag en by design; the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- Tests: the three Microsoft.UI-free files (Model/Source/ViewModel) are linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj
  alongside the sibling SchemaDriftPage links (the bare WinUI view is excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI); 40
  DiskForecastPageTests assert the projection, parsers, the four-state matrix (+503), the client request shaping
  and the diagnostics/registration headlessly.

